    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d169-a1">

                <pb facs="0255" n="181" sameAs="frus:frus1866p2/pg181"/>

                <head>Count Mandeström to Mr.
                        Campbell.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Upsala,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-09-19"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 19, 1866</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: I have taken the orders of the King,
                    and his Majesty has been pleased to tell me that he wished you would present to
                    him Mr. Fox, as well as the commanders of the two vessels of the United States,
                    on Saturday next, the 22d instant, at 11 o’clock a. m., at his private rooms at
                    the palace of Stockholm.</p>
                <p>I think it well to tell you that the intention of his Majesty is to visit the
                    Miantonomoh on Saturday at 3 o’clock p. m., and to see on Sunday at dinner the
                    American officers you can choose to present to his Majesty, and of whom you have
                    kindly promised to give me a list on my return to Stockholm on Friday.</p>
                <p>Yours, most truly,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>MANDERSTEÖM.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
